gt; by &lt;a href="http://www.zazzle.co.uk/doodle_m*"&gt;doodle_m&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Shop for another &lt;a href="http://www.zazzle.co.uk/postcards?rf=238269554763928881"&gt;postcard design&lt;/a&gt; from Zazzle&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>White Indian Tiger</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/white-indian-tiger/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Mar 2011 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/white-indian-tiger/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 8 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 13 links are now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;White Tiger at a park near Bangalore.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/5505583875/" title="White Tiger Orton Effect by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm6.static.flickr.com/5094/5505583875_93d8b1e23f_z.jpg" width="640" height="538" alt="White Tiger Orton Effect" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;This has the &lt;a href="http://www.google.co.uk/url?sa=t&amp;source=web&amp;cd=1&amp;ved=0CBsQFjAA&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FOrton_(photography)&amp;ei=nkR_TYqUKYiEhQeUq_yrBw&amp;usg=AFQjCNFUptzSKmyu4L1aqgYVkuv5pahVLw&amp;sig2=2XB-E-6Y3N-SjOlncDdsGw"&gt;Orton Effect&lt;/a&gt; applied the original image can be seen below&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/5199623632/" title="DSC_2741 by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm6.static.flickr.com/5129/5199623632_074b9515a5_t.jpg" width="100" height="67" alt="DSC_2741" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Buy this picture &lt;a href="http://www.zazzle.co.uk/white_tiger_postcard-239713919655514809?gl=doodle_m&amp;amp;type=standard_postcard"&gt;White Tiger Postcard&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href="http://www.zazzle.co.uk/white_tiger_tshirt-235902645734378572?gl=doodle_m&amp;amp;style=kids_basic_tshirt&amp;amp;color=white&amp;amp;size=y_m&amp;amp;context=brianna&amp;amp;view=front"&gt;White Tiger T-shirt&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alastair Montgomery&amp;rsquo;s Photography&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Experiments in HDR</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/experiments-in-hdr/</link><pubDate>Thu, 15 Jul 2010 12:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/experiments-in-hdr/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 4 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 8 links are now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Here is my first real attempt at an HDR image, taken from three shot with a 1.3+- exposure bracketing.&lt;br /&gt;The foreground is a bit blurry as the wind was moving the plants and I wasn&amp;rsquo;t using a tripod, notes for next time.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4776720007/" title="Ripon Sunset HDR by Alastair Montgomery, on Flickr"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm5.static.flickr.com/4102/4776720007_2035ce11c9.jpg" width="500" height="342" alt="Ripon Sunset HDR" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;After converting from the RAW files I arranged the three images as separate layers in Photoshop.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;The layers where arranged as +1.3 exposure,normal,-1.3.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Then I added layer masks to the top two layers.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Painting on the top layer mask I removed the &amp;ldquo;burnt out&amp;rdquo; sections from the top layers so the correctly exposed section from the layer below showed through.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;I repeated this again on the second layer.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;I ran a low Gaussian blur on the layer masks to soften the edges of the masks to reduce the halo effect.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;li&gt;Then I merge each layer into the one below to create the finished image.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;p style="text-align: center;"&gt;&lt;span style="font-size:85%;"&gt;&lt;b&gt;Alastair Montgomery&amp;rsquo;s Photography&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>12/52 Lunch Andy Warhol Style</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/1252-lunch-andy-warhol-style/</link><pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2009 13:32:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/1252-lunch-andy-warhol-style/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 3 links is now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4077908126/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2569/4077908126_6f03a4a9d9_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 0px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/4077908126/"&gt;12/52 Lunch Andy Warhol Style&lt;/a&gt; &lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br clear="all" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Part of my lunch time apple taken with my LG RENOIR, edited in The Gimp&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>8/52 Tweet Deck Overload</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/852-tweet-deck-overload/</link><pubDate>Thu, 08 Oct 2009 10:51:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/852-tweet-deck-overload/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3992766526/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm4.static.flickr.com/3093/3992766526_1ef9d2b7f1_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style=" margin-top: 0px;font-size:0.9em;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3992766526/"&gt;8/52 Tweet Deck Overload&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;p&gt;Taken with my LG Renoir, played with in Photoshop&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Making of Circuit Lady</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/making-of-circuit-lady/</link><pubDate>Wed, 01 Jul 2009 11:41:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/making-of-circuit-lady/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note:&lt;/strong&gt; 1 of this post&amp;rsquo;s 4 links is now broken — mostly deleted or made-private Flickr photos, dead Flickr &lt;code&gt;farmN&lt;/code&gt; subdomains, and defunct feed-syndication infrastructure. Left as originally published.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3677536671/" title="photo sharing"&gt;&lt;img src="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2461/3677536671_0a77c0a4cb_m.jpg" alt="" style="border: solid 2px #000000;" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 0.9em; margin-top: 0px;"&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/3677536671/"&gt;Making of Circuit Lady&lt;/a&gt; &lt;br /&gt;Originally uploaded by &lt;a href="http://www.flickr.com/people/doodle_m/"&gt;Alastair Montgomery&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br clear="all" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;Photo edit I did a while ago using some stock images and The Gimp.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;a href="http://farm3.static.flickr.com/2461/3677536671_38c29081eb_o.jpg"&gt;View it full sized&lt;/a&gt;&